# preempted-run-keeps-segment-base: pins that a Run preempted by a Fuel Slice
# is saved mid-Segment, continues after the restore exactly where it was cut
# (a `continue` stretch, not a restart), keeps its Fuel used so far, and that
# its segment base survives the save: the Limit Fault it hits after the
# restore rolls `n` back to 0, undoing the `add 1 to n` made before the save.
#
# This case pins its Fuel figures, and the faulting instruction, from Cost
# Model 0 (spec/data/costs.toml). Up to the loop, counter/r1 spends
#   dispatch, one clause tried (clause)          4
#   const 1, store, load-var, load (const, slot) 4
#   add, a 1-digit result (arithmetic, 3 + 1/8)  4
#   store-var n                                  2   = 14,
# then counter:10, `jump 0010`, at 1 Fuel a turn. With a slice of 100 the
# slice is spent at exactly 100, so the Run is preempted there. After the
# restore it goes on to its fuelPerRun of 1000, 900 more, and the next
# `jump` can't be covered: the fault is at counter:10, pos 9:3.
# Allocation is the one number `add` builds (16), and the state figure is
# `n` alone once the Run has ended (a number, 16).

> load counter identity=35995d29e61aab89b857a07142c6a89d9bdf1804a9825c5dca6dab155108a406

# The slice cuts the Run in the middle of its first Segment.
> deliver d1 to=counter message=spin
> pump clock=2026-09-30T10:00:00Z fuel-slice=100
preempt counter/r1 start delivery=d1 handler=spin clause=1 by=slice fuel=100 alloc=16
pumped state=sliced fuel=100

# Saved while preempted. Nothing is pending, so the restore lists nothing to
# settle.
> save s1
> restore from=s1 fingerprint=ad91f7b2c9f884dd88232d9a1e3479d5b7a13d16fc1c5825e670e6f1652b03a0 mode=full

# No slice now. The Run continues from the instruction it was cut before, on
# the Fuel it had left (1000 - 100), and faults. `rollback=[n]` shows the
# segment base came through the save: `n` goes back to 0.
> pump clock=2026-09-30T10:00:01Z
fault counter/r1 limit=fuel at=counter:10 pos=9:3 rollback=[n]
seg counter/r1 continue fuel=900 alloc=0 state=16 end=fault
run counter/r1 outcome=limit-fault delivery=d1 handler=spin limit=fuel fuel=1000 alloc=16
pumped state=idle fuel=900

> vars
vars counter n=0
